# 2. Getting Started

## 2.1 System Access and Login
Access to the Voucher Processing & Authorization System is strictly governed by Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). 

To access the system:
1. Navigate to the secure portal via your designated corporate web browser.
2. Enter your authorized User ID and Password on the SSO (Single Sign-On) login screen.
3. Upon successful authentication, the system will securely retrieve your profile and dynamically render the dashboard. 
*Note: For security and compliance purposes, your session is actively monitored. If the system detects extended periods of inactivity, your session will automatically time out, requiring you to log in again. Furthermore, any active Voucher ID (VID) locks you hold will be instantly released upon closing the browser tab.*

## 2.2 Navigating the Dashboard
Because the system operates on strict segregation of duties, your navigation menu will only display the modules authorized for your specific role. 

Below is the access matrix defining the available screens for each operational role:

**A. Roles: TCS GLIF & HB GLIF**
These roles act primarily as the "Makers" (and intermediate Checkers) of the financial pipeline.
*   **Voucher Posting:** Initiate new batches using assigned VIDs (Supports both Manual Entry and Bulk Excel Upload).
*   **Voucher Posting Status:** Track the lifecycle, workflow progress, and audit history of submitted batches.
*   **Voucher Authorization:** Review, approve, or reject pending batches submitted by other makers.
*   **Search Category-Wise Voucher:** Query and view vouchers categorized by specific business units.
*   **Search CGL / Branch / Asset & Liabilities:** Access inquiry screens to safely search and validate General Ledgers, Branch Codes, and Asset/Liability configurations.

**B. Role: SBI GLIF**
This role acts as the "Administrator" and "Final Approver" of the financial pipeline.
*   **Request Voucher:** Create and configure the master Voucher IDs (VIDs), defining descriptions and issue categories.
*   **View Request Voucher:** Audit and manage existing VID configurations.
*   **Voucher Authorization:** Perform the ultimate final approval on batches and dictate the final Execution Time (Immediate or Scheduled).
*   **Search Category-Wise Voucher:** Query and view categorized vouchers.
*   **Search CGL / Branch / Asset & Liabilities:** Access inquiry screens to validate codes.

**C. Role: TCS IMPL (Author Role)**
This role functions specifically as an "Author" or "Initiator" within the system.
*   Users with the TCS IMPL role share the core posting capabilities required to author new entries, generate batches, and utilize the inquiry screens to validate their inputs before routing them to the checker queue.

## 2.3 Important Business Rules & Constraints
To maintain the highest level of financial data integrity, the system hard-codes several non-bypassable constraints. Please keep the following rules in mind while using the system:

*   **Strict Balancing Rule:** For every batch submitted, the Total Debits must perfectly equal the Total Credits. The system enforces this balance at a granular level: it must balance *per Branch* and *per Currency*.
*   **Minimum Row Constraint (Manual Entry):** A manual voucher posting cannot be submitted with a single entry. The system requires a minimum of two (2) transactional rows (e.g., one Debit and one Credit) to satisfy accounting principles. These baseline rows cannot be deleted from the grid.
*   **Self-Approval Block (Segregation of Duties):** A user is physically restricted from authorizing (Approving or Rejecting) any batch that they created. If a Maker navigates to the Authorization screen, the "Proceed to Action" button for their own batches will be disabled with a security violation warning.
*   **Amount Limitations:** Financial amounts cannot be zero. Input fields enforce a strict limit of up to 16 integer digits and exactly 4 decimal places.
*   **Remarks Constraints:** Action remarks and row-level remarks are strictly mandatory. They must be between 2 and 30 characters long. To prevent data corruption, the system only accepts alphanumeric characters, spaces, and the following symbols: `/ & ( ) , . -`.
*   **End of Day (EOD) Blackout:** If the core banking system initiates its End of Day (EOD) batch processing, the Voucher Posting screens will be temporarily locked. Users will see a prominent warning, and new transactions cannot be entered until the EOD cycle successfully completes.
